1Novel locus defined by no known published variants within 1Mb (+/-500 Kb) of the lead SNP.							
2Known locus defined by previously identified signal(s) within a 1Mb region (+/-500Kb) for the indicated trait.							
3Human Genome Organisation approved gene names, unless otherwise indicated.							
"4Expression quantitative trait loci (eQTLs) and splice quantitative trait loci (sQTLs) were identified from the Genotype-Tissue Expression (GTEx) Project.  One row per significant QTL. GTEx was supported by the Common Fund of the Office of the Director of the National Institutes of Health, and by NCI, NHGRI, NHLBI, NIDA, NIMH, and NINDS. The data used for the analyses described in this manuscript were obtained from the GTEx Portal on 09/28/20.  Osteoclast eQTL results are from a single cohort eQTL study of 158 human osteoclast-like cell cultures that were differentiated from peripheral blood mononuclear cells. Those indicated met multiple testing correction for the number of lead GWAS SNPs per trait. http://www.gefos.org/?q=content/human-osteoclast-eqtl-2018-2020
